## Stop Hook Safety
Any stop hook that triggers tool calls MUST include a maximum retry count (max 3) and graceful failure handling. If the hook's required tool call fails due to API limits, context overflow, or prompt-too-long errors, the hook must exit cleanly and log the failure rather than retrying infinitely.

## Automated Observer/Checkpoint Sessions
Automated memory observation and progress checkpoint sessions must: (1) check API quota availability before starting, (2) fail fast with a written summary if quota is exhausted, (3) never retry more than 3 times on any error. If the primary session completed work but the observer cannot record it, save a plaintext note locally instead.

